WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.980
Film Courage: Can we talk about the difference
in creating a fascinating protagonist for

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.279
film versus television?

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:07.080
Or maybe it’s the same?

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:15.710
Dan Calvisi: For film I think it’s going
to be affected by that closed ending because

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:25.050
their arc is going to arc over the course
of this 90 to 120 minute film or 90 to 110

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.800
page screenplay.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.619
And then it’s going to end basically and
that’s where we’re going to leave the

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:30.900
character.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:37.770
Whereas a TV protagonist, they have to be
able to go through various arcs over the course

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.840
of years, you know?

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.830
It may be for 10 seasons so there needs to
be the potential for that kind of growth.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:48.710
Now you don’t need to know what’s going
to happen to this character to 10 seasons

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.050
but it would be good to know the basics of
what will happen like in the first two or

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.830
three seasons for example.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.480
Film Courage: Any examples of characters you
can provide?

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:04.960
Dan Calvisi: Well if you give your protagonist
a lot of emotional baggage, then there’s

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.670
going to be a lot to unpack over time.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.119
Something like Carrie from Homeland.

00:01:11.119 --> 00:01:19.740
She is bipolar and she is reckless in her
behavior and she starts an affair with this

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.329
guy who she is supposed to be tracking that’s
a potential bad guy in Season One.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:29.369
So she’s kind of a mess and so there’s
definitely going to be drama with her going

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.369
forward.

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:32.499
Or Don Draper from Mad Men.

00:01:32.499 --> 00:01:38.499
He has the secret personality from the past
and he has this secret that he’s keeping…What

00:01:38.499 --> 00:01:39.640
his true identity?

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.999
That’s always a risk to come out to destroy
him.

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:50.799
So if you keep some kind of element there,
some kind of Achilles' heel always there and

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:55.499
ready to destroy them, then you are going
to get a lot of seasons of material out of

00:01:55.499 --> 00:01:56.499
that hero.

00:01:56.499 --> 00:02:03.069
Film Courage: Let’s talk about for a feature
film because you said that there’s closure.

00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:05.329
Can you give examples of an interesting protagonist?

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:07.549
It can be from a current film or not?

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:12.069
Dan Calvisi: Yes…a classic example of a
great character arc would be Indiana Jones

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:13.610
and Raiders of the Los Ark.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:18.950
You know the first Indiana Jones film his
arc is to accept the supernatural.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.870
He doesn’t believe in anything supernatural
or spiritual.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.830
He doesn’t believe in God.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:29.650
So when he gets this mission to find the Ark
of the Covenant, he just thinks it’s relic,

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:30.650
you know?

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.950
He doesn’t think it’s actually something
that could have any kind of power.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:40.220
His final fruition of the Ark is when he respects,
let say “God’s Power,” and the power

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:44.970
of the Ark and he shuts his eyes and tells
Marion to shut her eyes once the Ark has been

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:51.260
open and the power of the Ark kills all the
bad guys but does not hurt him and Marion

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:55.860
because they’ve respected God and not looked
at the face of God.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.829
So it’s not just him in a fight, you know?

00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:03.110
You would think it’s an action movie, non-stop
action would be him fighting the head bad

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.110
guy.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.120
It’s not at all and that’s what makes
it an interesting choice for the character

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.190
and to close the film it’s him respecting
the spiritual world.

